      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u give me a summary of the debate over school vouchers? like why do people think they're good for kids and why do people hate them?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure. Proponents of school vouchers argue they promote competition and provide low-income families with the opportunity to choose better schools, thus improving overall educational quality. They believe vouchers can empower parents and offer a means to tailor education to children's needs, enhancing academic success and personal growth. Critics, however, argue that vouchers divert needed funds from public schools, potentially narrowing resources for those who remain in the public system. Additionally, they fear vouchers may lead to a two-tier education system, where affluent families can access better schools while others face declining public education quality. This debate hinges on contrasting values around educational equity, school funding, and governmental role in education.",
